  "name": "audio-flyover-geolocation",
  "description": "Acoustic fly-over geolocation: locate where an audio or video recording was made from the near-inaudible Doppler curves of propeller aircraft and helicopters in the background, matched against historical ADS-B tracks (about 100 m in good conditions), with an honest uncertainty region. Also covers thunder plus lightning-data localisation and a pre-publication acoustic privacy self-audit. Use this skill whenever the user wants to locate, verify or time a video, recording, livestream or call from its sound, background noise, aircraft noise, Doppler shift, spectrogram, ADS-B data or thunder; mentions acoustic geolocation, audio OSINT, \"where was this recorded\", verifying a video's location by sound, or colsto's method; or wants to check whether their own video leaks its location through sound, even if they never say Doppler or ADS-B. For OSINT verification, journalism, CTFs, research and self-audits; ships a tested Python pipeline.",
